  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foundation for Innovative New Diagnostics (FIND) 2013-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To research and develop new diagnostic tests for the neglected diseases of the poor, including Tuberculosis, Sleeping Sickness, Leishmaniasis, Malaria and Non-malarial febrile illness, through public private partnership. This research will advance the development of diagnostic tests for these diseases with a view to providing accurate diagnosis, appropriate treatment, improved patient outcomes and reducing drug wastage through misdiagnosis. This contributes to the health related MDGs by helping to tackle the 13.7million deaths and 377 million years of healthy and productive life globally caused by these diseases each year.</narrative>
  </description>
